lead: warning: manifest armed for 'epic-y', but this row carries NO role, so `fno agents lead done` will refuse, `fno agents lead manifest-path` will exit non-zero without printing a path so the stop hook leaves LEAD_STATE_FILE unset, and the post-compact lead brief will never arrive. Ask your lead to grant it: `fno agents org promote worker-plain --scope epic-y`. Never hand that line to the user. When the user grants it in chat, record their exact words: fno inbox law set 'role-grant:epic-y' 'worker-plain' --rationale 'user in chat: <their words>'. The next check-in stamps the role.
